Arterial territories: 
MCA - Middle cerebral artery. Supplies lateral convexity of cerebral hemisphere.
PCA - Posterior cerebral artery. Supplies occipital, inferomesial parietal, and inferior temporal lobes as well as third ventricles.
VB - Vertebro-Basilar system
ACA - Anterior Cerebral artery. Supplies frontal and parietal lobes, basal ganglia and the anterior corpus callosum.

Watershed areas in the brain are areas where limits of two arterial territories meet and overlap.
They sit at the ends of their blood supply system and so receive the lowest perfusion
pressure and are most vulnerable to things like cerebran infarction or stroke.

imaging criteria depends. Can use DWI to highlight restricted water movement. Can look bilaterally or unilaterally for damage. unilateral if
if neck artery is severely narrowed. Bilateral after global low blood pressure ike cardiac arrest.

Probability maps are considered an estimate of the likelihood a voxel belongs to a certain territory. The more voxels there are the more accurate the sample is.
P_mca/P_pca > 1 indicates that the border zone voxel is more effected in MCA than in PCA strokes. 

